    "created_at": "2019-09-03T03:21:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-03T03:22:49Z",
    "body": "I think my inclination would be to default to no numbers as well. Personally, if I see a diverged status, I know what I need to do: pull, then push (or fetch/rebase/push or whatever). Knowing how many ahead/behind I am is nice-to-have, but I can `git status` if that information is going to affect my decisions.\r\n\r\nIf an advanced user wants to see the ahead/behind count, they can read the docs and find that option in the git section. If a beginning user is confused by the numbers, they don't have the same luxury (at least, not until `explainer` comes out)",
